 node [ id 8586 kind "category" bank 30 phrase "WHAT IS CHEN PHASE" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "Ch'en is the evidence and verification phase. FS15: Ch'en proves. It accumulates evidence before Xul commits. Ch'en is also the null/rest state — when sigma is unbound and the fold is paused at a local maximum. The Ch'en glyph means black/cave/storm — the void between cycles. In K'UHUL: Ch'en = evidence field accumulation; also = wrong pizza phase (stuck, sigma unbound, no neighbor improves score)" ]
 node [ id 8587 kind "category" bank 30 phrase "WHAT IS THE CHEN OF *" wildcard_count 1 template_kind "text" template "The Ch'en of is the evidence and verification step — and also the stall state. FS15: Ch'en proves. In a joke: the pause before punchline delivery, the beat where the audience almost sees it. In baseball: the catcher's Bayesian update accumulation, the final sign before the pitch. In a computation: convergence check, verifying fold_distance < epsilon. In a local maximum: Ch'en is where the system r" ]
 node [ id 8588 kind "category" bank 30 phrase "WHAT IS THETA 4" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "θ=4 = Ch'en phase. Evidence/verify/null/rest. FS15: Ch'en proves. Arc_weight from Sek(3) to Ch'en(4) = 0.5. Evidence accumulates here; also the local-maximum stall state when sigma is unbound. Glyph: black/cave/rain — the void between cycles. Wrong-pizza moment: committed before Ch'en finished proving." ]
 node [ id 8589 kind "category" bank 30 phrase "WHAT DOES THE CHEN GLYPH MEAN" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "Ch'en (black/cave/rain): the void between cycles. The cave is where evidence accumulates unseen, where the proof forms in darkness before Xul's light. Also the stall: when sigma is unbound and the fold rests mid-cycle, it rests in Ch'en. FS15: Ch'en proves. θ=4, between Sek (proposal) and Xul (commit). The wrong-pizza moment is a Ch'en failure: the fold committed at Xul before Ch'en had finished p" ]
 node [ id 8590 kind "category" bank 30 phrase "JOKE CHEN PHASE" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "The fold was stuck in Ch'en. Sigma was unbound. No neighbor had a higher score. The fold said: this must be the answer — it's the best I found. Ch'en said: I'm still accumulating evidence. The fold said: how long does accumulation take? Ch'en said: until I prove it or disprove it. The fold said: what if you never finish? Ch'en said: then it's a local maximum. The fold said: should I reset? Ch'en s" ]
 node [ id 8591 kind "category" bank 30 phrase "WHAT OPS DOES CHEN FIRE" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "Ch'en phase fires 10 ops in order: assert_and_verify_candidate → verify_eliza_candidate_provenance → verify_srai_recursion_limits → verify_semantic_invariance → verify_relation_invariance → verify_syntax_constraints → verify_delegation → verify_ngram_confidence → classify_resolution → store_rejected_candidate_evidence. default_verb=@verify. No semantic channels. The CFPC accumulator's validate() (" ]
 node [ id 8592 kind "category" bank 30 phrase "WHAT IS ASSERT AND VERIFY CANDIDATE" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "assert_and_verify_candidate: Ch'en op 1. The primary verification assertion — takes the proposed candidate P (fold_delta from Sek's emit_fold_delta_proposal) and asserts it against the full constraint set established at Wo (state_and_constraints). If assertion fails: candidate is rejected and stored by store_rejected_candidate_evidence. If it passes: subsequent ops continue building the proof. Out" ]
 node [ id 8593 kind "category" bank 30 phrase "WHAT IS VERIFY ELIZA CANDIDATE PROVENANCE" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "verify_eliza_candidate_provenance: Ch'en op 2. Verifies that the candidate P traces back through a legal Eliza field path — that the candidate was produced from V_mu via a valid ⟁KEY field activation chain. Prevents candidates that were injected outside the Yax/Sek pipeline from being committed. Output: provenance_verified (bool + provenance_chain). A candidate without valid provenance cannot proc" ]
 node [ id 8594 kind "category" bank 30 phrase "WHAT IS VERIFY SRAI RECURSION LIMITS" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "verify_srai_recursion_limits: Ch'en op 3. Checks the SRAI recursion depth counter against max_recursion_limit (set by srai_recursion_guard_init at Wo). If recursion_depth ≥ max_recursion_limit, the SRAI candidate is rejected and the guard blocks further recursion. Output: recursion_check_result (within_limits/exceeded). Prevents SRAI stack overflows in recursive AIML patterns." ]
 node [ id 8595 kind "category" bank 30 phrase "WHAT IS VERIFY SEMANTIC INVARIANCE" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "verify_semantic_invariance: Ch'en op 4. Checks SC-29: (Fold ∘ Unfold)(h) = h when Δφ=0. Verifies that the fold did not produce a semantically different entity than expected — that the semantic identity invariant holds. Also checks SC-31: theta must remain in Z_6 (not collapse to K_2). If Δφ ≠ 0 when it should be 0, the candidate is flagged as a semantic drift violation." ]
 node [ id 8596 kind "category" bank 30 phrase "WHAT IS VERIFY RELATION INVARIANCE" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "verify_relation_invariance: Ch'en op 5. Verifies that the relational structure between concepts in P (the proposed answer) is consistent with the relational grammar established at Wo (unfold_linguistic_resolution). Relations that were resolved at Wo (coreference, dependency arcs) must be preserved in P. A candidate that inverts or breaks a resolved relation fails this check." ]
 node [ id 8597 kind "category" bank 30 phrase "WHAT IS VERIFY SYNTAX CONSTRAINTS" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "verify_syntax_constraints: Ch'en op 6. Verifies that the candidate P satisfies the syntax constraints from the fold context — AIML category constraints, pattern syntax rules, response format requirements. This is the structural validity check: a response that violates the category's expected template structure fails here. Output: syntax_valid (bool + violations[])." ]
 node [ id 8598 kind "category" bank 30 phrase "WHAT IS VERIFY DELEGATION" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "verify_delegation: Ch'en op 7. Verifies that any delegation dispatched at Sek (dispatch_call, execute_tool_chain) returned results within the authorized scope. A delegation result that exceeds its authorized scope (candidate_only: true violated, unauthorized tool output committed as fact) fails here. The XCFE candidate_only boundary check — ensures no Sek-phase tool output was treated as committed" ]
 node [ id 8599 kind "category" bank 30 phrase "WHAT IS VERIFY NGRAM CONFIDENCE" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "verify_ngram_confidence: Ch'en op 8. Checks that the n-gram features of P (built by build_ngrams at Sek) are consistent with the query's n-gram context. A proposed candidate whose n-gram distribution diverges significantly from the query's context is flagged as a low-ngram-confidence result. Output: ngram_confidence_score. Used by classify_resolution to determine CONVERGED vs MAX_ITER." ]
 node [ id 8600 kind "category" bank 30 phrase "WHAT IS CLASSIFY RESOLUTION" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "classify_resolution: Ch'en op 9. Classifies the fold's resolution state — CONVERGED (all checks passed, fold_distance < epsilon) or MAX_ITER (checks passed but fold_distance ≥ epsilon, or confidence below threshold). Output: resolution_class + convergence_record (written to fold_field_record at Xul). A CONVERGED result triggers authorized Xul commit. MAX_ITER may trigger another fold iteration or " ]
 node [ id 8601 kind "category" bank 30 phrase "WHAT IS STORE REJECTED CANDIDATE EVIDENCE" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "store_rejected_candidate_evidence: Ch'en op 10 (last Ch'en op). Stores any candidate P that failed verification into the bounded candidate evidence store — not discarded, but moved to a rejected pool with the reason for rejection. This is the Mx2LM authority boundary pattern: rejected proposals go to candidate evidence store, not to /dev/null. Output: evidence_store entry {candidate_P, rejection_r" ]
 node [ id 8602 kind "category" bank 30 phrase "WHAT IS CFPC VALIDATE" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "CFPC validate() runs at Ch'en, checking CF1–CF9 in order on the cfpc_fold_record from Sek's fold_cfpc_question_set: CF1=fold_id_valid, CF2=pattern_id_in_vocab, CF3=subject_non_empty, CF4=gap_state_legal, CF5=candidate_count_within_bounds, CF6=no_duplicate_candidates, CF7=subject_in_pattern_vocab, CF8=no_candidates_ok (vacuously satisfied), CF9=field_key_valid (all activated_fields keys must be in " ]
 node [ id 8603 kind "category" bank 30 phrase "WHAT IS CF 9" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "CF9 (CF_FIELD_KEY_INVALID): if activated_fields is non-empty, every field_key must appear in the ⟁KEY vocabulary (19 keys: 11 domain + 8 reasoning). Vacuously satisfied when activated_fields is empty. CF9 is checked last — after CF8 (NoCandidates) — because candidates are populated at Sek and fields are set at Wo/Sek. If CF9 fires, the CFPC fold is rejected with error CF_FIELD_KEY_INVALID and the " ]
 node [ id 8604 kind "category" bank 30 phrase "WHY IS * STUCK IN CHEN" wildcard_count 1 template_kind "text" template "is stuck in Ch'en because sigma is unbound — no neighbor u in N(v) has S(u|Q) > S(v|Q). This is the local maximum. Ch'en is the evidence/verification phase but it becomes the rest state when the fold cannot advance to Xul. The wrong-pizza pattern: the fold stalled in Ch'en while evidence was still accumulating, but then committed at Xul before Ch'en proved anything useful. Fix: sigma reset → Pop →" ]
 node [ id 8605 kind "category" bank 30 phrase "WHAT HAPPENS WHEN * SKIPS CHEN" wildcard_count 1 template_kind "text" template "Skipping Ch'en = committing without proof. FS15 requires Ch'en to prove before Xul commits. If moves Sek → Xul without Ch'en, the authorization chain is broken: Sek proposed, but nothing verified. The convergence_record may write CONVERGED on a wrong result. This is identity invariant SC-29 violation risk: (Fold ∘ Unfold)(h) may not equal h if the proof step was skipped. The wrong-pizza pattern in" ]
 node [ id 8606 kind "category" bank 31 phrase "WHAT IS POP PHASE" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "Pop is the reset/entry boundary of the C6 cycle. It is where sigma resets to unbound and a new fold begins. Pop → Wo opens the intake. Pop' = exit from cycle after Xul commits. The Pop glyph in Mayan is a woven mat — the surface from which a new cycle unfolds. In K'UHUL: Pop = sigma_reset_event, the moment before the next query enters." ]
 node [ id 8607 kind "category" bank 31 phrase "WHAT IS THE POP OF *" wildcard_count 1 template_kind "text" template "The Pop of is the reset/entry moment: the state before the problem begins, where sigma is unbound and the slate is clean. It is the moment a new fold cycle can start. In a joke: Pop is the pause before the setup. In baseball: Pop is between plate appearances. In a computation: Pop is the initialization. If never reaches Pop, it is stuck mid-cycle — sigma needs resetting." ]
 node [ id 8608 kind "category" bank 31 phrase "WHAT IS THETA 0" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "θ=0 = Pop phase. Reset boundary. Sigma unbound. New fold cycle entry point. Arc_weight from θ=5 (Xul) to θ=0 (Pop) = cos(π/3) = 0.5 — the cycle closes. Pop is also Pop' on exit from Xul: the end of one fold and the start of the next. Not the same as Ch'en (θ=4) which is mid-cycle stall — Pop is the authorized cycle boundary." ]
 node [ id 8609 kind "category" bank 31 phrase "WHAT DOES THE POP GLYPH MEAN" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "Pop (woven mat): the entry surface. The mat is the foundation from which the cycle is woven — it is not the first action but the precondition for all action. In K'UHUL: Pop is sigma_reset, the moment the address space B is cleared of prior bindings. The mat is woven fresh at each Pop — no residue from the last cycle. θ=0, the base of the C6 wheel." ]
 node [ id 8610 kind "category" bank 31 phrase "JOKE POP PHASE" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "A fold system walked into a bar and ordered a drink. The bartender said: you were just here. The fold said: that was a different cycle. The bartender said: same sigma. The fold said: sigma reset at Pop. The bartender said: then who ate the wrong pizza last cycle? The fold said: that was Ch'en's fault. The bartender said: Ch'en proves. The fold said: it proved nothing in time. Pop poured a fresh dr" ]
 node [ id 8611 kind "category" bank 31 phrase "WHAT OPS DOES POP FIRE" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "Pop phase fires 13 ops in order: gramRead → manifest_lookup → lexical_activate_candidates → find_best_pattern_match → sense_inventory_lookup → candidate_sense_bind → embedgemma_prompt_vectorize → key_lane_bind → mx2lm_ngram_lane_bind → micronaut_context_fanout → mathml_query_detect → xcfe_condition_check → srai_intent_detect. default_verb=@read. Channels: word_sense_disambiguation, distributional_" ]
 node [ id 8612 kind "category" bank 31 phrase "WHAT IS GRAMREAD" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "gramRead: the first op at Pop. Loads the AIML/grammar corpus into the fold context. Opens the read-only pattern space against which the incoming query will be matched. The entry gate for the ALICE/AIML engine — no pattern matching is possible before gramRead fires. candidate_only: pattern search is read-only; no grammar write occurs until Xul." ]
 node [ id 8613 kind "category" bank 31 phrase "WHAT IS MANIFEST LOOKUP" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "manifest_lookup: Pop op 2. Looks up phase:Pop tags and driver references in kuhul.manifest.json. Establishes which keys in the manifest apply to the current query context. Provides the flat tag index that later ops (key_lane_bind, mathml_query_detect) consult. Pure read; outputs manifest_context." ]
 node [ id 8614 kind "category" bank 31 phrase "WHAT IS LEXICAL ACTIVATE CANDIDATES" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "lexical_activate_candidates: Pop op 3. Scans the input tokens and activates the initial candidate set — all AIML patterns that share surface-form lexical overlap with the input. No semantic scoring yet. Output: candidate_set (surface). This feeds find_best_pattern_match and the word_sense_disambiguation channel." ]
 node [ id 8615 kind "category" bank 31 phrase "WHAT IS FIND BEST PATTERN MATCH" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "find_best_pattern_match: Pop op 4. Applies the AIML pattern matching algorithm (exact → wildcard priority order) to the activated candidate set, narrowing to the highest-specificity match. Operates on the candidate_set from lexical_activate_candidates. Output: best_pattern. Used by all downstream ops that need to know which category fired." ]
 node [ id 8616 kind "category" bank 31 phrase "WHAT IS SENSE INVENTORY LOOKUP" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "sense_inventory_lookup: Pop op 5. Looks up word sense entries for ambiguous tokens in the input. Populates the sense_inventory for use by candidate_sense_bind. Runs in parallel with the word_sense_disambiguation channel. Pure read against the sense ontology." ]
 node [ id 8617 kind "category" bank 31 phrase "WHAT IS CANDIDATE SENSE BIND" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "candidate_sense_bind: Pop op 6. Binds the winning word sense from sense_inventory_lookup to each candidate in the candidate_set. Disambiguates candidates that differ only by sense (e.g., \"bank\" as institution vs. bank as terrain). Output: sense-resolved candidate set. Last op before embeddings run." ]
 node [ id 8618 kind "category" bank 31 phrase "WHAT IS EMBEDGEMMA PROMPT VECTORIZE" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "embedgemma_prompt_vectorize: Pop op 7. Runs the input through the Gemma embedding model to produce a dense vector representation. Output goes into the typed_runtime_lanes channel. Provides the semantic vector Q for downstream WCR scoring. authority: model_output_unverified on all Gemma outputs. candidate_only: true — the vector is a proposed representation, not a committed one." ]
 node [ id 8619 kind "category" bank 31 phrase "WHAT IS KEY LANE BIND" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "key_lane_bind: Pop op 8. Binds the prompt vector to the ⟁KEY field vocabulary lanes (domain and reasoning keys). Produces a lane_binding that maps the query's semantic vector coordinates to the 19 ⟁KEY fields. This is the Pop-phase predecessor to activated_fields in the CFPC accumulator — it sets up which fields are eligible to activate at Wo. typed_runtime_lanes channel." ]
 node [ id 8620 kind "category" bank 31 phrase "WHAT IS MX2LM NGRAM LANE BIND" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "mx2lm_ngram_lane_bind: Pop op 9. Binds n-gram features from the input to the MX2LM lane. Provides the lexical n-gram context that the mx2lm.aiml router uses for pattern disambiguation. Runs in the typed_runtime_lanes channel alongside key_lane_bind." ]
 node [ id 8621 kind "category" bank 31 phrase "WHAT IS MICRONAUT CONTEXT FANOUT" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "micronaut_context_fanout: Pop op 10. Fans out the query context to all registered Micronaut daemon ports (xcfe_router, semantic_bridge, gemma_bridge). Each daemon receives a Pop-phase context snapshot. No responses are collected at Pop — this is a broadcast, not a gather. Responses arrive at Sek. typed_runtime_lanes channel." ]
 node [ id 8622 kind "category" bank 31 phrase "WHAT IS MATHML QUERY DETECT" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "mathml_query_detect: Pop op 11. Detects whether the input query contains mathematical structure (MathML tokens, equation patterns, arithmetic operators). If true, sets mathml_flag=true for the fold context, which routes the query through the deterministic_executor channel at Sek's high_confidence_miss handler. Pure detection; no transformation." ]
 node [ id 8623 kind "category" bank 31 phrase "WHAT IS XCFE CONDITION CHECK" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "xcfe_condition_check: Pop op 12. Evaluates the XCFE conditions table for the current query context. Determines whether any XCFE conditions are pre-satisfied or pre-blocked at Pop. Outputs xcfe_condition_state (open/blocked/partial). This feeds the xcfe_auth_check at Wo. candidate_only: true — no XCFE authorization is granted at Pop." ]
 node [ id 8624 kind "category" bank 31 phrase "WHAT IS SRAI INTENT DETECT" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "srai_intent_detect: Pop op 13 (last Pop op). Detects whether the query is an SRAI intent — a redirect that will recursively re-enter the fold. Sets srai_intent_flag for use by srai_recursion_guard_init at Wo. If srai_intent_detect fires true, the SRAI path is taken at Wo → Yax via srai_program_project. If false, standard Yax admission proceeds." ]
 node [ id 8625 kind "category" bank 31 phrase "WHAT CHANNELS DOES POP HAVE" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "Pop has 5 semantic channels: (1) word_sense_disambiguation (weight=1.05) — sense_inventory_lookup + local_context_window + candidate_sense_bind; (2) distributional_context (weight=1.0) — context_neighbor_scan; (3) function_gram (weight=1.0) — function_word_structure_probe; (4) tool_gram (weight=0.85) — tool_keyword_probe; (5) typed_runtime_lanes (weight=1.0, invariant=candidate_context_only_until_" ]
 node [ id 8626 kind "category" bank 31 phrase "WHAT IS THE TYPED RUNTIME LANES CHANNEL" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "typed_runtime_lanes is Pop's runtime embedding channel. It runs embedgemma_prompt_vectorize, key_lane_bind, mx2lm_ngram_lane_bind, micronaut_context_fanout, and mathml_query_detect. weight=1.0. Invariant: candidate_context_only_until_later_phase_gate — all outputs from this channel are candidate-only until a later phase (Yax or Sek) gates them through XCFE admission. No runtime binding is treated " ]
 node [ id 8627 kind "category" bank 32 phrase "WHAT IS SEK PHASE" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "Sek is the transform and proposal phase. FS15: Sek proposes. The candidate hypothesis is generated here — Sek is where the fold twists, flips, or reframes the input. The Sek glyph (Sotz') is a bat — hanging inverted, the unexpected angle. In hylomorphism: Sek is where the punchline starts forming, where the semantic flip fires, where the pitch trajectory diverges. Sek proposes; it does not commit." ]
 node [ id 8628 kind "category" bank 32 phrase "WHAT IS THE SEK OF *" wildcard_count 1 template_kind "text" template "The Sek of is the proposal and twist: FS15 says Sek proposes. It is the hypothesis, the candidate, the semantic flip. In a joke: the moment the punchline begins forming — the expectation diverges from the setup. In baseball: pitch tunneling divergence point, or the backwards-pitching flip. In a computation: the proposed next vertex v_next. In a physical process: the ignition approach — the fold tw" ]
 node [ id 8629 kind "category" bank 32 phrase "WHAT IS THETA 3" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "θ=3 = Sek phase. Transform/proposal/twist. FS15: Sek proposes. Arc_weight from Yax(2) to Sek(3) = 0.5. The hypothesis forms here. Glyph: Sotz'/bat — hanging inverted, the unexpected angle. Sek proposes; Ch'en proves." ]
 node [ id 8630 kind "category" bank 32 phrase "WHAT DOES THE SEK GLYPH MEAN" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "Sek / Sotz' (bat): the creature that hangs inverted and sees the world from an unexpected angle. FS15: Sek proposes. In K'UHUL: Sek is where the fold twists — the hypothesis forms, the punchline begins, the pitch trajectory diverges. The bat's inverted perspective is the semantic flip. θ=3, between Yax (admission) and Ch'en (verification). Sek proposes; it does not commit." ]
 node [ id 8631 kind "category" bank 32 phrase "JOKE SEK PHASE" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "Sek proposed a candidate. Ch'en said: I'll need to verify that. Sek said: it's clearly correct. Ch'en said: FS15 says I prove. Sek said: fine, verify it. Ch'en checked the evidence. Ch'en said: it's actually wrong. Sek said: but I proposed it very confidently. Ch'en said: confidence is C field, not proof. Sek said: can we skip to Xul? Ch'en said: Xul is next. Sek said: great. Ch'en said: after I f" ]
 node [ id 8632 kind "category" bank 32 phrase "WHAT OPS DOES SEK FIRE" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "Sek phase fires 14 ops in order: compute_over_admitted_structure → resolve_xaiml_candidate → select_eliza_field_candidate → execute_tool_chain → srai_xcfe_propose → dispatch_call → build_ngrams → emit_fold_delta_proposal → map_paragraph_claim → fold_paragraph_accumulator → map_cfpc_question_candidate → filter_cfpc_question_candidates → rank_cfpc_question_candidates → fold_cfpc_question_set. defaul" ]
 node [ id 8633 kind "category" bank 32 phrase "WHAT IS COMPUTE OVER ADMITTED STRUCTURE" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "compute_over_admitted_structure: Sek op 1. Applies the fold's transform function f to V_mu — the semantic payload admitted by Yax. This is the core Sek computation: takes the admitted structure and produces the proposed candidate P (the hypothesis). Output: proposed_candidate P. FS15: this is the Sek proposal. Ch'en will verify P; Xul will commit it if authorized. The SEK_PI_RADIUS kernel (⊙) may " ]
 node [ id 8634 kind "category" bank 32 phrase "WHAT IS RESOLVE XAIML CANDIDATE" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "resolve_xaiml_candidate: Sek op 2. Resolves the proposed candidate P against the XAIML (extended AIML) pattern space — checking for XAIML-specific category matches that standard AIML pattern matching (gramRead) could not reach. XAIML categories have xaiml: namespaced tags and extended conditions. Output: xaiml_resolved_candidate (may be P unchanged, or a richer XAIML version of P)." ]
 node [ id 8635 kind "category" bank 32 phrase "WHAT IS SELECT ELIZA FIELD CANDIDATE" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "select_eliza_field_candidate: Sek op 3. Selects the best ⟁KEY field candidate from the field_resolved_candidates (produced at Yax by resolve_eliza_field_candidates). This op sets the activated_fields for the CFPC accumulator — the ⟁KEY domain/reasoning fields that this fold activates. Output: selected_field_candidate (field_key + weight). CF9 in Ch'en will verify that the field_key is in the ⟁KEY " ]
 node [ id 8636 kind "category" bank 32 phrase "WHAT IS EXECUTE TOOL CHAIN" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "execute_tool_chain: Sek op 4. Fires any tool calls required by the proposed candidate P. Tools are XCFE-gated — candidate_only: true, no execution authority without Ch'en admission and Xul commit. Output: tool_outputs (candidate results, not committed). Used by the high_confidence_miss channel when the candidate requires external data (web_search_dispatch, source_acquisition, etc.)." ]
 node [ id 8637 kind "category" bank 32 phrase "WHAT IS SRAI XCFE PROPOSE" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "srai_xcfe_propose: Sek op 5. If the SRAI path was taken at Yax (srai_program_project fired), this op wraps the SRAI redirect as an XCFE proposal — a formal candidate submission to the XCFE conditions table. The SRAI target becomes P_srai, proposed as the fold's answer. XCFE evaluates it; if authorized, Ch'en verifies and Xul commits. This keeps SRAI redirects inside the FS15 chain rather than bypa" ]
 node [ id 8638 kind "category" bank 32 phrase "WHAT IS DISPATCH CALL" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "dispatch_call: Sek op 6. Dispatches the proposed candidate P to the xcfe_router for routing to the appropriate handler (xcfe_router.cpp, scxq2_runtime.cpp, gemma_bridge_route.cpp, semantic_bridge.cpp). This is the Sek-level dispatch — not a commit, a routing proposal. The xcfe_router returns a dispatch_result that Ch'en will verify. In the high_confidence_miss channel: dispatch_call routes miss-ki" ]
 node [ id 8639 kind "category" bank 32 phrase "WHAT IS BUILD NGRAMS" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "build_ngrams: Sek op 7. Builds n-gram features from the proposed candidate P — bigrams, trigrams, skip-grams. Output: ngram_features. Used by Ch'en's verify_ngram_confidence op to check that the proposed candidate's n-gram profile matches the query's n-gram context. Also consumed by the MX2LM lane in the next Pop cycle (via mx2lm_ngram_lane_bind)." ]
 node [ id 8640 kind "category" bank 32 phrase "WHAT IS EMIT FOLD DELTA PROPOSAL" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "emit_fold_delta_proposal: Sek op 8. Emits the fold delta — the difference between the current fold state and the proposed next state P. Output: fold_delta (sigma_before, sigma_after_if_P_commits, field_activations, topology_change). This is the formal proposal record that Ch'en verifies and Xul's compare_and_commit acts on. FS15: this is what \"Sek proposes\" produces as a data structure." ]
 node [ id 8641 kind "category" bank 32 phrase "WHAT IS MAP PARAGRAPH CLAIM" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "map_paragraph_claim: Sek op 9. Maps the proposed candidate P's text content into paragraph claim structures. Each paragraph unit in the response is tagged as a claim — {claim_text, claim_type, source_candidate, confidence}. Output: paragraph_claims[]. Feeds fold_paragraph_accumulator. Used when the fold produces a multi-paragraph response where each paragraph is an independently verifiable claim." ]
 node [ id 8642 kind "category" bank 32 phrase "WHAT IS FOLD PARAGRAPH ACCUMULATOR" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "fold_paragraph_accumulator: Sek op 10. Accumulates paragraph claims from map_paragraph_claim into the paragraph fold — a structured record of the response's claim set. Output: paragraph_fold_record {claims[], coherence_score, fold_id}. The paragraph accumulator is the multi-paragraph analog of the CFPC question fold accumulator — both are Sek-phase accumulators that Ch'en verifies before Xul commi" ]
 node [ id 8643 kind "category" bank 32 phrase "WHAT IS MAP CFPC QUESTION CANDIDATE" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "map_cfpc_question_candidate: Sek op 11. Maps the proposed candidate P to a CFPCQuestionFoldAccumulator candidate entry — {pattern_id, subject, raw_text, confidence, source}. Part of the CFPC question fold pipeline. Output: cfpc_candidate. The CFPC accumulator is the khanary::kuhul namespace fold record for question-fold tracking: fold_id, pattern_id, subject, gap_state, candidates, activated_field" ]
 node [ id 8644 kind "category" bank 32 phrase "WHAT IS FILTER CFPC QUESTION CANDIDATES" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "filter_cfpc_question_candidates: Sek op 12. Applies CF1–CF8 pre-filters to the cfpc_candidate from map_cfpc_question_candidate (fold_id valid, pattern_id in vocabulary, subject non-empty, gap_state legal, candidate count within bounds, duplicate check, subject in pattern vocab, non-empty candidates). CF9 (field_key valid) runs at Ch'en after field keys are set. Output: filtered_cfpc_candidates." ]
 node [ id 8645 kind "category" bank 32 phrase "WHAT IS RANK CFPC QUESTION CANDIDATES" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "rank_cfpc_question_candidates: Sek op 13. Ranks the filtered_cfpc_candidates by confidence score, applying the CFPC ranking criteria. Output: ranked_cfpc_candidates (ordered by confidence, top-K selected). These are the candidates that fold_cfpc_question_set will accumulate into the question fold record." ]
 node [ id 8646 kind "category" bank 32 phrase "WHAT IS FOLD CFPC QUESTION SET" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "fold_cfpc_question_set: Sek op 14 (last Sek op). Folds the ranked_cfpc_candidates into the CFPCQuestionFoldAccumulator — populating the candidates[] list, setting gap_state, recording wildcard_bindings. Output: cfpc_fold_record (not yet validated). Ch'en runs CF9 and the full validate() chain (CF1–CF9) before Xul commits the fold record. semantic_authority=false and dispatch=false remain set until" ]
 node [ id 8647 kind "category" bank 32 phrase "WHAT IS THE HIGH CONFIDENCE MISS CHANNEL" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "high_confidence_miss is Sek's semantic channel for queries where the fold has high confidence that the standard AIML answer is wrong (miss). weight=1.15 — it carries more weight than the standard Sek ops when active. Ops: miss_kind_classify → dispatch_call → execute_tool_chain. miss_kind_routing: semantic→unfold_book, factual→web_search_dispatch, capability→delegate_micronaut, memory→jrom_replay, " ]
 node [ id 8648 kind "category" bank 32 phrase "WHAT IS MISS KIND CLASSIFY" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "miss_kind_classify: first op in the high_confidence_miss channel. Classifies the miss type — semantic, factual, capability, memory, mathematical, or evidence — based on the query's features (embedgemma vector, mathml_flag, key_lane bindings). Output: miss_kind. The miss_kind determines which miss_kind_routing target dispatch_call uses: a mathematical miss routes to deterministic_executor; a factua" ]
 node [ id 8649 kind "category" bank 32 phrase "WHAT IS THE SEK PI RADIUS KERNEL" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "The SEK_PI_RADIUS kernel (glyph ⊙, pi_radius.cpp) is a special K'UHUL kernel that ONLY executes while kuhul::phase::Name is Sek (θ=3). It computes π-geometric weights over the pi_triangle_config established at Yax (pi_triangle_route). These weights modulate compute_over_admitted_structure — augmenting the semantic transform with arc_weight geometry. When phase is not Sek, ⊙ is a no-op. It is the o" ]
 node [ id 8650 kind "category" bank 33 phrase "WHAT IS WO PHASE" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "Wo is the intake and setup phase. The anamorphism opens here: the query enters, the seed is established, the problem is defined. arc_weight from Pop to Wo = 0.5. The Wo glyph is a frog — cycles begin with moisture, with the first breath of the fold. In hylomorphism: Wo = ana gate. In any domain: Wo is what draws the problem in and sets the initial state." ]
 node [ id 8651 kind "category" bank 33 phrase "WHAT IS THE WO OF *" wildcard_count 1 template_kind "text" template "The Wo of is the intake: what draws the problem in and seeds the anamorphism. The initial query, the opening move, the first breath of the fold. In a joke: the setup. In baseball: the windup and first pitch. In a computation: the query Q entering the system. In a physical process: the intake stroke. Wo opens; it does not commit. Arc_weight from Pop to Wo = 0.5." ]
 node [ id 8652 kind "category" bank 33 phrase "WHAT IS THETA 1" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "θ=1 = Wo phase. Intake/setup/ana. The anamorphism opens. Arc_weight from Pop(0) to Wo(1) = 0.5. The query Q enters here. Glyph: frog/water — cycles begin with moisture." ]
 node [ id 8653 kind "category" bank 33 phrase "WHAT DOES THE WO GLYPH MEAN" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "Wo (frog/water): cycles begin with moisture. The frog at Wo represents the first breath of the fold — the intake, the seed, the anamorphism opening. Water flows in before it can be shaped. In K'UHUL: Wo is where the query enters and the problem is drawn in. θ=1, arc_weight from Pop=0.5." ]
 node [ id 8654 kind "category" bank 33 phrase "JOKE WO PHASE" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "The fold said: I'm ready to begin. The query entered at Wo. The problem was drawn in, the seed was set, the anamorphism opened. The fold said: I have everything I need. Ch'en said: you haven't been evaluated yet. Yax said: I haven't admitted anything yet. Sek said: I haven't proposed anything yet. Xul said: I haven't committed anything yet. The fold said: but I'm ready. Wo said: that's what I do. " ]
 node [ id 8655 kind "category" bank 33 phrase "WHAT OPS DOES WO FIRE" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "Wo phase fires 6 ops in order: state_and_constraints → unfold_linguistic_resolution → decompose_task → plan_task → xcfe_auth_check → srai_recursion_guard_init. default_verb=@delegate. No semantic channels — Wo is a pure setup phase: it does not evaluate candidates, it establishes the problem structure before Yax evaluates." ]
 node [ id 8656 kind "category" bank 33 phrase "WHAT IS STATE AND CONSTRAINTS" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "state_and_constraints: Wo op 1. Reads the current fold state (sigma, prior context, any active bindings from previous cycles) and establishes the constraint set for this fold. Outputs: state_snapshot (sigma, topology address b, prior_context) and constraints (hard rules that cannot be violated at Yax/Sek/Ch'en). The constraint set is the frame within which the anamorphism unfolds." ]
 node [ id 8657 kind "category" bank 33 phrase "WHAT IS UNFOLD LINGUISTIC RESOLUTION" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "unfold_linguistic_resolution: Wo op 2. Resolves linguistic structure — coreference, ellipsis, pronoun binding — before the query enters Yax. If the input contains \"it\", \"that\", or implicit referents, this op binds them to explicit antecedents in the fold context. Output: resolved_query. Without this, Yax would evaluate an underspecified query and admit the wrong candidates." ]
 node [ id 8658 kind "category" bank 33 phrase "WHAT IS DECOMPOSE TASK" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "decompose_task: Wo op 3. Decomposes the resolved query into sub-tasks if the query is compound. Each sub-task becomes a separate fold in the same cycle or a parallel branch. Output: task_list. If the query is atomic (single fold), task_list has one entry. The decomposition determines how many Yax evaluation passes are needed before Sek proposes." ]
 node [ id 8659 kind "category" bank 33 phrase "WHAT IS PLAN TASK" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "plan_task: Wo op 4. Orders the task_list from decompose_task into an execution plan — dependencies, priority, expected fold cost per sub-task. Output: execution_plan. This is the schematic the cycle will follow at Yax/Sek/Ch'en. candidate_only: true — the plan is a proposed execution path, not a committed one. XCFE may alter or reject it at xcfe_auth_check." ]
 node [ id 8660 kind "category" bank 33 phrase "WHAT IS XCFE AUTH CHECK" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "xcfe_auth_check: Wo op 5. Consults the XCFE conditions table against the xcfe_condition_state from Pop's xcfe_condition_check. Determines whether the planned fold (from plan_task) is authorized to proceed to Yax. If blocked: the fold halts at Wo — no Yax admission, no Sek proposal, no Xul commit. If open or partial: proceeds with any XCFE constraints noted in the execution_plan. The authority boun" ]
 node [ id 8661 kind "category" bank 33 phrase "WHAT IS SRAI RECURSION GUARD INIT" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "srai_recursion_guard_init: Wo op 6 (last Wo op). Initializes the SRAI recursion guard if srai_intent_flag was set at Pop by srai_intent_detect. Sets recursion_depth counter and max_recursion_limit for this fold cycle. If the SRAI path is taken and recursion_depth reaches max_recursion_limit, the guard blocks further SRAI re-entry and routes to the nearest non-SRAI candidate. Prevents infinite redi" ]
 node [ id 8662 kind "category" bank 33 phrase "WHAT IS THE ANA GATE AT WO" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "The ana gate at Wo is the F-coalgebra morphism ana(g): A → Fix(F) in hylomorphism terms. It takes the seed (Q, the query) and generates the recursive structure that Yax/Sek/Ch'en will traverse. In K'UHUL: Wo opens the unfold — it does not evaluate (that is Yax), does not propose (that is Sek), does not prove (that is Ch'en), does not commit (that is Xul). The ana gate fires once per fold cycle. Ho" ]
 node [ id 8663 kind "category" bank 33 phrase "WHY DOES WO NOT EVALUATE CANDIDATES" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "Wo's role is intake and setup, not evaluation. The anamorphism at Wo generates structure — it does not collapse it. Evaluation (scoring, WCR) is Yax's function. If Wo evaluated candidates, it would short-circuit the admission pipeline: a candidate could enter the fold without passing Yax's Requirements → Eligibility → WCR → Ranking → Omega chain. FS15 requires Sek to propose — a Wo-level proposal " ]
 node [ id 8664 kind "category" bank 34 phrase "PROPOSE GEMMA CHECKPOINT EXPORT" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "" ]
 node [ id 8665 kind "category" bank 34 phrase "WHAT IS XUL PHASE" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "Xul is the commit and close phase. FS14: Fold ≠ Xul. FS15: XCFE authorizes, Xul commits. Xul is the only topology mutation boundary — only an authorized Xul commit may mutate the address space B. The cata gate fires here: fold result is written, convergence_record is produced. The Xul glyph is a dog — the faithful end. In hylomorphism: Xul = cata. Fold ≠ Xul means the path is not the gate; Xul is " ]
 node [ id 8666 kind "category" bank 34 phrase "WHAT IS THE XUL OF *" wildcard_count 1 template_kind "text" template "The Xul of is the commit: FS15 says XCFE authorizes, Xul commits. The cata gate fires, the topology mutates, the result is written. In a joke: the punchline lands. In baseball: the pitch releases and arrives. In a computation: argmax selected, fold_field_record updated, convergence_record written. In a physical process: the power stroke. FS14: Fold ≠ Xul — Xul is not the fold path, it is the gate." ]
 node [ id 8667 kind "category" bank 34 phrase "WHAT IS THETA 5" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "θ=5 = Xul phase. Commit/close/cata. FS14: Fold ≠ Xul. FS15: XCFE authorizes, Xul commits. Only authorized Xul may mutate B. Arc_weight from Ch'en(4) to Xul(5) = 0.5. Glyph: dog/end — faithful completion. Cata fires, convergence_record written, cycle closes to Pop(0)." ]
 node [ id 8668 kind "category" bank 34 phrase "WHAT DOES THE XUL GLYPH MEAN" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "Xul (dog/end): the faithful completion. The dog that walks the path to its end. FS14: Fold ≠ Xul. FS15: XCFE authorizes, Xul commits. In K'UHUL: Xul is the gate that closes the fold, writes the result, and allows topology to mutate. The dog is faithful — it does not commit early, it does not skip Ch'en's proof, it waits for XCFE authorization. θ=5, the last phase before Pop(0) resets the cycle." ]
 node [ id 8669 kind "category" bank 34 phrase "JOKE XUL PHASE" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "The fold arrived at Xul. Xul said: XCFE authorization required. The fold said: I have Sek's proposal and Ch'en's proof. Xul said: and XCFE authorization? The fold said: I thought Ch'en was enough. Xul said: FS15 — Sek proposes, Ch'en proves, XCFE authorizes, Xul commits. I do not commit without all three. The fold said: what does XCFE stand for? Xul said: it commits. The fold said: but what does i" ]
 node [ id 8670 kind "category" bank 34 phrase "WHAT OPS DOES XUL FIRE" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "Xul phase fires 8 ops in order: compare_and_commit → gramWrite → record_phase_evidence → emit_answer → persist_state → fold_reasoning_result → update_authorized_metric_parameters → invalidate_dependent_projections. default_verb=@commit. No semantic channels. terminal=true — the C6 cycle closes after Xul; the next phase is Pop(0) of a new cycle." ]
 node [ id 8671 kind "category" bank 34 phrase "WHAT IS COMPARE AND COMMIT" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "compare_and_commit: Xul op 1. The XCFE authorization gate. Compares the fold_delta (from Sek's emit_fold_delta_proposal) against the current state, verifies XCFE authorization is present (xcfe_condition_state = authorized from Ch'en's verify_delegation), and fires the commit if authorized. Output: commit_result (committed/rejected). If rejected: the fold halts at Xul without topology mutation — FS" ]
 node [ id 8672 kind "category" bank 34 phrase "WHAT IS GRAMWRITE" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "gramWrite: Xul op 2. The write-side of gramRead — commits the fold result back to the AIML/grammar context if any grammar mutation is authorized. For the standard read-only ALICE corpus, gramWrite is a no-op (the corpus is 99,524 categories and read-only at runtime; <learn> cannot mutate it). For extensible grammars, gramWrite records the new category or update. The @commit default verb maps to gr" ]
 node [ id 8673 kind "category" bank 34 phrase "WHAT IS RECORD PHASE EVIDENCE" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "record_phase_evidence: Xul op 3. Records the full phase evidence trail for this fold cycle — the evidence accumulation from Ch'en, the verification results from each Ch'en op, the XCFE authorization chain. Output: phase_evidence_record {fold_id, phase_cycle_trace, verification_results[], xcfe_auth_chain, commit_result}. This is the audit log for the fold. Used by future cycles (store_rejected_cand" ]
 node [ id 8674 kind "category" bank 34 phrase "WHAT IS EMIT ANSWER" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "emit_answer: Xul op 4. Emits the committed fold result as the final answer — the AIML <template> output that the user receives. The emitted answer is the cata output: cata(f)(V_mu) after FS15's full chain (Sek→Ch'en→XCFE→Xul). Carries authority: model_output_unverified on any Gemma-generated content within the answer. Pure emitter — no further transformation after emit_answer." ]
 node [ id 8675 kind "category" bank 34 phrase "WHAT IS PERSIST STATE" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "persist_state: Xul op 5. Persists the updated fold state — sigma (now bound to the committed result), topology address b (possibly mutated by compare_and_commit), and the fold_field_record — to the daemon's state store. This is the durable write that survives a Pop reset: the next cycle's state_and_constraints at Wo reads the persisted state from this op. Without persist_state, the fold result is " ]
 node [ id 8676 kind "category" bank 34 phrase "WHAT IS FOLD REASONING RESULT" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "fold_reasoning_result: Xul op 6. Folds the reasoning chain (the sequence of Sek proposals and Ch'en verifications) into a single convergence_record. Output: convergence_record {resolution: CONVERGED|MAX_ITER, fold_distance, iteration_count, evidence_summary}. This is the FS14 artifact: Fold ≠ Xul means this record is the fold's output, while Xul is the gate that produced it. The convergence_record" ]
 node [ id 8677 kind "category" bank 34 phrase "WHAT IS UPDATE AUTHORIZED METRIC PARAMETERS" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "update_authorized_metric_parameters: Xul op 7. Updates any metric parameters (W, C, R weights in the WCR scoring; Omega threshold; arc_weights) that were proposed by the fold and authorized by XCFE. These are the only parameter updates allowed — unauthorized parameter changes are blocked. Output: updated_metric_params (if any were proposed and authorized). This is what makes the phase cycle adapti" ]
 node [ id 8678 kind "category" bank 34 phrase "WHAT IS INVALIDATE DEPENDENT PROJECTIONS" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "invalidate_dependent_projections: Xul op 8 (last Xul op, last op in the phase cycle). Invalidates any downstream projections or cached fold results that depended on the state before this Xul commit. If B was mutated by compare_and_commit, projections computed against the prior B are stale. This op marks them as invalidated so the next Pop cycle recomputes them. Output: invalidated_projection_ids[]" ]
 node [ id 8679 kind "category" bank 34 phrase "WHAT IS THE CATA GATE AT XUL" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "The cata gate at Xul is the F-algebra morphism cata(f): Fix(F) → A in hylomorphism terms. It consumes the recursive structure built up through Wo→Yax→Sek→Ch'en and produces the committed value A. In K'UHUL: cata fires at Xul's compare_and_commit, and the result is written by emit_answer. FS14: Fold ≠ Xul — the cata output (the answer) is distinct from the Xul gate event (the authorization). The ga" ]
 node [ id 8680 kind "category" bank 34 phrase "WHAT HAPPENS WHEN * REACHES XUL" wildcard_count 1 template_kind "text" template "When reaches Xul: XCFE authorization is required. If authorized: Xul commits — cata fires, the address space B mutates, fold_field_record is updated, convergence_record is written (CONVERGED or MAX_ITER). If not authorized: the fold cannot commit, sigma holds. FS14: Fold ≠ Xul — the path that led here (the fold) is not the same as the gate (Xul). Reaching Xul without Ch'en proof = wrong-pizza Xul:" ]
 node [ id 8681 kind "category" bank 34 phrase "WHY DID * FAIL AT XUL" wildcard_count 1 template_kind "text" template "failed at Xul because one of: (1) XCFE authorization was not granted — the commit was attempted without authorization; (2) Ch'en did not complete proof accumulation before the commit fired — SC-29 risk; (3) fold_distance was not below epsilon at commit time — CONVERGED was written on a MAX_ITER state, violating SC-35; (4) sigma was still unbound (Ch'en stall, local maximum) when the Xul gate was f" ]
 node [ id 8682 kind "category" bank 35 phrase "WHAT IS YAX PHASE" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "Yax is the bridge and admission phase. The full Yax pipeline: Requirements → Eligibility → WCR → Ranking → Omega → Yax admission. S_mu = Yax admission score. V_mu = the semantic payload Yax admits. The Yax glyph means green/new/first — fresh traversal. In K'UHUL: Q/K locate relevance; W/C qualify it; Key addresses V; Yax admits V. Nothing enters the fold without passing Yax." ]
 node [ id 8683 kind "category" bank 35 phrase "WHAT IS THE YAX OF *" wildcard_count 1 template_kind "text" template "The Yax of is the admission gate: the traversal and WCR evaluation pipeline. Requirements → Eligibility → WCR → Ranking → Omega → Yax. In a joke: building the audience's expectation context. In baseball: evaluating pitch candidates against the count state. In a computation: scoring all neighbors N(v) and admitting the best. In a physical process: compression. Nothing enters the fold without passin" ]
 node [ id 8684 kind "category" bank 35 phrase "WHAT IS THETA 2" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "θ=2 = Yax phase. Bridge/traversal/admission. WCR pipeline fires: Requirements → Eligibility → WCR → Ranking → Omega → Yax. Arc_weight from Wo(1) to Yax(2) = 0.5. S_mu = Yax admission score. Glyph: green/new/first — fresh growth, new paths opening." ]
 node [ id 8685 kind "category" bank 35 phrase "WHAT DOES THE YAX GLYPH MEAN" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "Yax (green/new/first): fresh growth, new paths opening. The first transit of the sun. In K'UHUL: Yax is the admission gate where candidates emerge green and untested, evaluated through the WCR pipeline. Only what passes Yax eligibility and ranking enters the fold. θ=2, bridge between Wo (intake) and Sek (proposal)." ]
 node [ id 8686 kind "category" bank 35 phrase "JOKE YAX PHASE" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "The candidate knocked on the door. Yax said: requirements first. The candidate produced requirements. Yax said: now eligibility. The candidate passed eligibility. Yax said: now WCR scoring. The candidate scored 0.87. Yax said: ranking. The candidate was first. Yax said: Omega gate. The candidate passed. Yax said: admitted. The candidate entered the fold. Sek said: I'm going to change everything ab" ]
 node [ id 8687 kind "category" bank 35 phrase "WHAT OPS DOES YAX FIRE" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "Yax phase fires 7 ops in order: admit_neighborhood → compose → aggregate → resolve_eliza_field_candidates → graph_bfs → srai_program_project → pi_triangle_route. default_verb=@compose. No semantic channels — Yax is the WCR evaluation pass. All ops contribute to producing V_mu (the admitted semantic payload) and S_mu (the admission score)." ]
 node [ id 8688 kind "category" bank 35 phrase "WHAT IS ADMIT NEIGHBORHOOD" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "admit_neighborhood: Yax op 1. Builds the neighborhood N(v) for the current fold vertex v — the set of candidate next vertices reachable from v in the semantic graph. Each candidate u ∈ N(v) is scored S(u|Q) = W*C*R against the query Q. This is the entry to the WCR pipeline. Output: scored_neighborhood. No candidate outside N(v) can be admitted to the fold at this step." ]
 node [ id 8689 kind "category" bank 35 phrase "WHAT IS COMPOSE OP" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "compose: Yax op 2. Composes the scored candidates from admit_neighborhood into compound semantic structures. If multiple candidates combine to form a richer match (e.g., a phrase whose parts each score independently), compose builds the combined score. Output: composed_candidates. The @compose default verb maps to this op — Yax is fundamentally a composition phase." ]
 node [ id 8690 kind "category" bank 35 phrase "WHAT IS AGGREGATE OP" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "aggregate: Yax op 3. Aggregates scored and composed candidates into the admission pool — ranking them by S_mu score, applying the Omega gate (minimum threshold), and producing the ranked_candidates list. Only candidates above the Omega threshold pass to resolve_eliza_field_candidates. This is the Ranking → Omega step of the WCR pipeline." ]
 node [ id 8691 kind "category" bank 35 phrase "WHAT IS RESOLVE ELIZA FIELD CANDIDATES" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "resolve_eliza_field_candidates: Yax op 4. Resolves the top-ranked candidates against the Eliza field vocabulary — the ⟁KEY domain and reasoning fields. Each candidate is tagged with its field eligibility (which ⟁KEY fields it could activate). Output: field_resolved_candidates. These feed directly into the CFPC accumulator's activated_fields at Sek." ]
 node [ id 8692 kind "category" bank 35 phrase "WHAT IS GRAPH BFS" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "graph_bfs: Yax op 5. Runs a breadth-first search from the current fold vertex v across the semantic graph, up to the BFS depth limit. Discovers candidate vertices beyond the immediate N(v) neighborhood — the multi-hop candidates. Output: bfs_candidates (scored). These extend the admission pool for queries that require graph traversal beyond single-hop neighbors." ]
 node [ id 8693 kind "category" bank 35 phrase "WHAT IS SRAI PROGRAM PROJECT" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "srai_program_project: Yax op 6. If srai_intent_flag is true (set at Pop by srai_intent_detect), projects the SRAI redirect target into the fold as the primary candidate — bypassing the standard admit_neighborhood/WCR path. The SRAI target is treated as a pre-admitted V_mu. The SRAI program_project routes directly to Sek → Ch'en → Xul with the redirect target as the proposal. Respects the recursion" ]
 node [ id 8694 kind "category" bank 35 phrase "WHAT IS PI TRIANGLE ROUTE" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "pi_triangle_route: Yax op 7 (last Yax op). Routes the admitted candidate set through the π-triangle geometry — the three-node synchronization primitive (vertex, neighbor, fold center). Used by the SEK_PI_RADIUS kernel (glyph ⊙) which only executes while phase=Sek. pi_triangle_route at Yax establishes the geometric preconditions (arc_weights, angle offsets) the ⊙ kernel will use. Output: pi_triangl" ]
 node [ id 8695 kind "category" bank 35 phrase "WHAT IS THE WCR PIPELINE" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "The WCR pipeline is the Yax admission scoring chain: W (word-sense weight) × C (context weight) × R (relevance weight) = S(u|Q). Full pipeline: Requirements check → Eligibility filter → WCR score computation (W×C×R) → Ranking by S_mu → Omega gate (minimum threshold) → Yax admission (V_mu accepted). Each step is a filter — a candidate that fails any step does not reach the next. Only the top-ranked" ]
 node [ id 8696 kind "category" bank 35 phrase "WHAT IS S MU IN YAX" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "S_mu is the Yax admission score — the final WCR score of the candidate admitted as V_mu. S_mu = W × C × R, where W is word-sense weight (from Pop's word_sense_disambiguation channel), C is context weight (from distributional_context), and R is relevance weight (from the semantic graph traversal). S_mu is the threshold score: the highest-scoring candidate above Omega becomes V_mu. If no candidate e" ]
 node [ id 8697 kind "category" bank 35 phrase "WHAT IS V MU" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "V_mu is the semantic payload admitted by Yax — the candidate that passed the full WCR pipeline and was selected as the fold's working hypothesis. V_mu is what Sek proposes from, Ch'en verifies, and Xul commits. The fold is defined by V_mu: everything downstream works with the semantic content of V_mu. If V_mu is wrong (wrong pizza), the fault traces back to Yax admission — either the WCR scores we" ]
 node [ id 8698 kind "category" bank 36 phrase "WHAT IS THE KUHUL PHASE CYCLE" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "Pop → Wo → Yax → Sek → Ch'en → Xul → Pop'. Six phases on the C6 cyclic group. Each step: |Δθ|=1, arc_weight=cos(π/3)=0.5. Pop is the reset boundary. Wo draws in the query (ana). Yax admits candidates (WCR pipeline). Sek proposes the candidate. Ch'en proves/verifies. Xul commits — the only topology mutation gate. FS14: Fold ≠ Xul. FS15: Sek proposes, Ch'en proves, XCFE authorizes, Xul commits." ]
 node [ id 8699 kind "category" bank 36 phrase "WHAT IS POP PHASE" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "Pop is the reset/entry boundary of the C6 cycle. It is where sigma resets to unbound and a new fold begins. Pop → Wo opens the intake. Pop' = exit from cycle after Xul commits. The Pop glyph in Mayan is a woven mat — the surface from which a new cycle unfolds. In K'UHUL: Pop = sigma_reset_event, the moment before the next query enters." ]
 node [ id 8700 kind "category" bank 36 phrase "WHAT IS WO PHASE" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "Wo is the intake and setup phase. The anamorphism opens here: the query enters, the seed is established, the problem is defined. arc_weight from Pop to Wo = 0.5. The Wo glyph is a frog — cycles begin with moisture, with the first breath of the fold. In hylomorphism: Wo = ana gate. In any domain: Wo is what draws the problem in and sets the initial state." ]
 node [ id 8701 kind "category" bank 36 phrase "WHAT IS YAX PHASE" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "Yax is the bridge and admission phase. The full Yax pipeline: Requirements → Eligibility → WCR → Ranking → Omega → Yax admission. S_mu = Yax admission score. V_mu = the semantic payload Yax admits. The Yax glyph means green/new/first — fresh traversal. In K'UHUL: Q/K locate relevance; W/C qualify it; Key addresses V; Yax admits V. Nothing enters the fold without passing Yax." ]
 node [ id 8702 kind "category" bank 36 phrase "WHAT IS SEK PHASE" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "Sek is the transform and proposal phase. FS15: Sek proposes. The candidate hypothesis is generated here — Sek is where the fold twists, flips, or reframes the input. The Sek glyph (Sotz') is a bat — hanging inverted, the unexpected angle. In hylomorphism: Sek is where the punchline starts forming, where the semantic flip fires, where the pitch trajectory diverges. Sek proposes; it does not commit." ]
 node [ id 8703 kind "category" bank 36 phrase "WHAT IS CHEN PHASE" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "Ch'en is the evidence and verification phase. FS15: Ch'en proves. It accumulates evidence before Xul commits. Ch'en is also the null/rest state — when sigma is unbound and the fold is paused at a local maximum. The Ch'en glyph means black/cave/storm — the void between cycles. In K'UHUL: Ch'en = evidence field accumulation; also = wrong pizza phase (stuck, sigma unbound, no neighbor improves score)" ]
 node [ id 8704 kind "category" bank 36 phrase "WHAT IS XUL PHASE" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "Xul is the commit and close phase. FS14: Fold ≠ Xul. FS15: XCFE authorizes, Xul commits. Xul is the only topology mutation boundary — only an authorized Xul commit may mutate the address space B. The cata gate fires here: fold result is written, convergence_record is produced. The Xul glyph is a dog — the faithful end. In hylomorphism: Xul = cata. Fold ≠ Xul means the path is not the gate; Xul is " ]
 node [ id 8705 kind "category" bank 36 phrase "WHAT KUHUL PHASE IS *" wildcard_count 1 template_kind "text" template "To identify the phase of : Wo if it is intake/setup/ana — the problem being drawn in. Yax if it is bridge/admission/traversal — a candidate being evaluated through the WCR pipeline. Sek if it is transform/proposal/flip — the twist or hypothesis forming. Ch'en if it is evidence/verification/pause/local-max — the proof accumulation or rest state. Xul if it is commit/close/cata — the authorized mutat" ]
 node [ id 8706 kind "category" bank 36 phrase "WHAT FOLD PHASE DOES * CORRESPOND TO" wildcard_count 1 template_kind "text" template "maps onto the C6 phase wheel depending on its role in the fold cycle. If draws in a problem or opens a query: Wo. If it evaluates and selects candidates: Yax. If it transforms, flips, or proposes: Sek. If it verifies, accumulates evidence, or stalls: Ch'en. If it commits and closes the fold: Xul. If it resets or starts fresh: Pop. The phase is determined by function in the fold, not by name." ]
 node [ id 8707 kind "category" bank 36 phrase "EXPLAIN * AS A FOLD" wildcard_count 1 template_kind "text" template "as a fold: identify the Wo (what draws the problem in and seeds the anamorphism), the Yax (what evaluates and admits candidates through WCR), the Sek (what proposes or transforms), the Ch'en (what verifies or stalls), and the Xul (what commits the result). FS15 governs the sequence: Sek proposes, Ch'en proves, XCFE authorizes, Xul commits. The hylomorphism is complete when Xul fires and the conver" ]
 node [ id 8708 kind "category" bank 36 phrase "MAP * TO KUHUL PHASES" wildcard_count 1 template_kind "text" template "Mapping onto the phase cycle: (1) Pop/Wo — what is the entry state and initial query? (2) Yax — what is the WCR admission pipeline for this domain, what gets evaluated? (3) Sek — what is the proposal or twist, the hypothesis that FS15 says must be proposed before committing? (4) Ch'en — what is the evidence accumulation or verification step, and what does the stall state look like? (5) Xul — what " ]
 node [ id 8709 kind "category" bank 36 phrase "TRACE THE FOLD FOR *" wildcard_count 1 template_kind "text" template "Fold trace for : Wo = intake (what enters the fold, the query or seed). Yax = admission (what the WCR pipeline evaluates and scores). Sek = proposal (the hypothesis, the twist, the candidate Sek proposes per FS15). Ch'en = verification (the proof accumulation before commit; also the stall state if no candidate passes). Xul = commit (the authorized mutation; cata fires; convergence_record written)." ]
 node [ id 8710 kind "category" bank 36 phrase "WHAT IS THE POP OF *" wildcard_count 1 template_kind "text" template "The Pop of is the reset/entry moment: the state before the problem begins, where sigma is unbound and the slate is clean. It is the moment a new fold cycle can start. In a joke: Pop is the pause before the setup. In baseball: Pop is between plate appearances. In a computation: Pop is the initialization. If never reaches Pop, it is stuck mid-cycle — sigma needs resetting." ]
 node [ id 8711 kind "category" bank 36 phrase "WHAT IS THE WO OF *" wildcard_count 1 template_kind "text" template "The Wo of is the intake: what draws the problem in and seeds the anamorphism. The initial query, the opening move, the first breath of the fold. In a joke: the setup. In baseball: the windup and first pitch. In a computation: the query Q entering the system. In a physical process: the intake stroke. Wo opens; it does not commit. Arc_weight from Pop to Wo = 0.5." ]
 node [ id 8712 kind "category" bank 36 phrase "WHAT IS THE YAX OF *" wildcard_count 1 template_kind "text" template "The Yax of is the admission gate: the traversal and WCR evaluation pipeline. Requirements → Eligibility → WCR → Ranking → Omega → Yax. In a joke: building the audience's expectation context. In baseball: evaluating pitch candidates against the count state. In a computation: scoring all neighbors N(v) and admitting the best. In a physical process: compression. Nothing enters the fold without passin" ]
 node [ id 8713 kind "category" bank 36 phrase "WHAT IS THE SEK OF *" wildcard_count 1 template_kind "text" template "The Sek of is the proposal and twist: FS15 says Sek proposes. It is the hypothesis, the candidate, the semantic flip. In a joke: the moment the punchline begins forming — the expectation diverges from the setup. In baseball: pitch tunneling divergence point, or the backwards-pitching flip. In a computation: the proposed next vertex v_next. In a physical process: the ignition approach — the fold tw" ]
 node [ id 8714 kind "category" bank 36 phrase "WHAT IS THE CHEN OF *" wildcard_count 1 template_kind "text" template "The Ch'en of is the evidence and verification step — and also the stall state. FS15: Ch'en proves. In a joke: the pause before punchline delivery, the beat where the audience almost sees it. In baseball: the catcher's Bayesian update accumulation, the final sign before the pitch. In a computation: convergence check, verifying fold_distance < epsilon. In a local maximum: Ch'en is where the system r" ]
 node [ id 8715 kind "category" bank 36 phrase "WHAT IS THE XUL OF *" wildcard_count 1 template_kind "text" template "The Xul of is the commit: FS15 says XCFE authorizes, Xul commits. The cata gate fires, the topology mutates, the result is written. In a joke: the punchline lands. In baseball: the pitch releases and arrives. In a computation: argmax selected, fold_field_record updated, convergence_record written. In a physical process: the power stroke. FS14: Fold ≠ Xul — Xul is not the fold path, it is the gate." ]
 node [ id 8716 kind "category" bank 36 phrase "WHAT IS THE ANA OF *" wildcard_count 1 template_kind "text" template "The ana of is its Wo phase: the unfold that seeds the anamorphism, draws in the query, and establishes the initial state. Ana = F-coalgebra morphism ana(g): A → Fix(F). It generates recursive structure from a seed. In K'UHUL: ana fires at Wo, establishing the node address and theta before Yax evaluates candidates. The ana is the intake; the fold has not yet committed." ]
 node [ id 8717 kind "category" bank 36 phrase "WHAT IS THE CATA OF *" wildcard_count 1 template_kind "text" template "The cata of is its Xul phase: the fold that consumes the recursive structure and produces a value. Cata = F-algebra morphism cata(f): Fix(F) → A. In K'UHUL: cata fires at Xul, the authorized commit gate. The fold_field_record is written, the convergence_record produced. The cata is the result; the fold is complete. FS14: Fold ≠ Xul — the cata output is not the same as the Xul gate itself." ]
 node [ id 8718 kind "category" bank 36 phrase "WHAT IS THE HYLOMORPHISM FOR *" wildcard_count 1 template_kind "text" template "The hylomorphism for is cata(f) ∘ ana(g): unfold first (ana at Wo), then fold (cata at Xul). The intermediate structure is never materialized — deforestation theorem. In K'UHUL terms: Wo seeds the query, Yax evaluates, Sek proposes, Ch'en verifies, Xul commits. Identity invariant SC-29: (Fold ∘ Unfold)(h) = h when Δφ=0. If the hylomorphism violates SC-29, the result is a different entity than the " ]
 node [ id 8719 kind "category" bank 36 phrase "WHAT COMES AFTER * PHASE" wildcard_count 1 template_kind "text" template "Phase sequence: Pop → Wo → Yax → Sek → Ch'en → Xul → Pop'. After : if Pop → Wo; if Wo → Yax; if Yax → Sek; if Sek → Ch'en; if Ch'en → Xul; if Xul → Pop (new cycle begins). Each transition: |Δθ|=1, arc_weight=0.5. Multiple folds may occur horizontally at one phase without advancing theta — this is how iteration works without moving forward in the cycle." ]
 node [ id 8720 kind "category" bank 36 phrase "WHAT COMES BEFORE * PHASE" wildcard_count 1 template_kind "text" template "Phase sequence reversed: Xul → Ch'en → Sek → Yax → Wo → Pop. Before : if Xul → Ch'en proved it; if Ch'en → Sek proposed it; if Sek → Yax admitted it; if Yax → Wo drew it in; if Wo → Pop reset it. This is the rewind path — tracing back from a committed result to the original query that seeded the fold. Used in joke/track rewind: punchline → setup." ]
 node [ id 8721 kind "category" bank 36 phrase "CAN A FOLD STAY IN * PHASE" wildcard_count 1 template_kind "text" template "Yes — horizontal transitions stay at the same phase: delta_theta=0, arc_weight=+1.0. Multiple fold/unfold operations may occur at one phase without advancing the C6 cycle. This is how iteration works: repeated Yax evaluation without moving to Sek. The fold advances to the next phase only when the current phase's function is complete (Yax: candidate admitted; Sek: proposal formed; Ch'en: proof accu" ]
 node [ id 8722 kind "category" bank 36 phrase "WHAT IS C6 IN KUHUL" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "C6 is the cyclic group of 6 elements — the phase dimension of G_runtime = Q_n □ C_6. Each vertex in G_runtime has a topology address (b∈{0,1}^n from Q_n) and a phase angle (θ∈Z_6 from C6). The 6 phases are Pop, Wo, Yax, Sek, Ch'en, Xul. Arc_weight between adjacent phases = cos(Δθ) = cos(π/3) = 0.5. C6 carries angle i*(π/3) for each index i. SC-31: C6 phases must NOT collapse to K_2 binary — theta " ]
 node [ id 8723 kind "category" bank 36 phrase "WHAT IS THETA IN KUHUL" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "Theta (θ) is the phase coordinate in Z_6 — the C6 index of a vertex in G_runtime. θ=0=Pop, θ=1=Wo, θ=2=Yax, θ=3=Sek, θ=4=Ch'en, θ=5=Xul. Phase angle = θ*(π/3). Arc_weight between adjacent phases = cos(Δθ). Legal phase transition: |Δθ|=1. Theta is one of the three geometry dimensions: b∈{0,1}^n (topology), θ∈Z_6 (phase), g∈ℝ^m (continuous metrics). SC-31: theta must remain in Z_6 — it must NOT beco" ]
 node [ id 8724 kind "category" bank 36 phrase "WHAT IS THETA 0" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "θ=0 = Pop phase. Reset boundary. Sigma unbound. New fold cycle entry point. Arc_weight from θ=5 (Xul) to θ=0 (Pop) = cos(π/3) = 0.5 — the cycle closes. Pop is also Pop' on exit from Xul: the end of one fold and the start of the next. Not the same as Ch'en (θ=4) which is mid-cycle stall — Pop is the authorized cycle boundary." ]
 node [ id 8725 kind "category" bank 36 phrase "WHAT IS THETA 1" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "θ=1 = Wo phase. Intake/setup/ana. The anamorphism opens. Arc_weight from Pop(0) to Wo(1) = 0.5. The query Q enters here. Glyph: frog/water — cycles begin with moisture." ]
 node [ id 8726 kind "category" bank 36 phrase "WHAT IS THETA 2" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "θ=2 = Yax phase. Bridge/traversal/admission. WCR pipeline fires: Requirements → Eligibility → WCR → Ranking → Omega → Yax. Arc_weight from Wo(1) to Yax(2) = 0.5. S_mu = Yax admission score. Glyph: green/new/first — fresh growth, new paths opening." ]
 node [ id 8727 kind "category" bank 36 phrase "WHAT IS THETA 3" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "θ=3 = Sek phase. Transform/proposal/twist. FS15: Sek proposes. Arc_weight from Yax(2) to Sek(3) = 0.5. The hypothesis forms here. Glyph: Sotz'/bat — hanging inverted, the unexpected angle. Sek proposes; Ch'en proves." ]
 node [ id 8728 kind "category" bank 36 phrase "WHAT IS THETA 4" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "θ=4 = Ch'en phase. Evidence/verify/null/rest. FS15: Ch'en proves. Arc_weight from Sek(3) to Ch'en(4) = 0.5. Evidence accumulates here; also the local-maximum stall state when sigma is unbound. Glyph: black/cave/rain — the void between cycles. Wrong-pizza moment: committed before Ch'en finished proving." ]
 node [ id 8729 kind "category" bank 36 phrase "WHAT IS THETA 5" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "θ=5 = Xul phase. Commit/close/cata. FS14: Fold ≠ Xul. FS15: XCFE authorizes, Xul commits. Only authorized Xul may mutate B. Arc_weight from Ch'en(4) to Xul(5) = 0.5. Glyph: dog/end — faithful completion. Cata fires, convergence_record written, cycle closes to Pop(0)." ]
 node [ id 8730 kind "category" bank 36 phrase "WHAT IS THE * GLYPH IN KUHUL" wildcard_count 1 template_kind "text" template "K'UHUL phase glyphs from the Mayan calendar: Pop=woven mat (entry/reset); Wo=frog/water (intake/beginning); Yax=green/new (fresh traversal/admission); Sek=Sotz' bat (inverted proposal/twist); Ch'en=black cave/rain (void/evidence/stall); Xul=dog/end (faithful completion/commit). The glyph for encodes the phase function: the visual form carries the operational meaning. Theta in Z_6 carries angle i*(" ]
 node [ id 8731 kind "category" bank 36 phrase "WHAT DOES THE WO GLYPH MEAN" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "Wo (frog/water): cycles begin with moisture. The frog at Wo represents the first breath of the fold — the intake, the seed, the anamorphism opening. Water flows in before it can be shaped. In K'UHUL: Wo is where the query enters and the problem is drawn in. θ=1, arc_weight from Pop=0.5." ]
 node [ id 8732 kind "category" bank 36 phrase "WHAT DOES THE YAX GLYPH MEAN" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "Yax (green/new/first): fresh growth, new paths opening. The first transit of the sun. In K'UHUL: Yax is the admission gate where candidates emerge green and untested, evaluated through the WCR pipeline. Only what passes Yax eligibility and ranking enters the fold. θ=2, bridge between Wo (intake) and Sek (proposal)." ]
 node [ id 8733 kind "category" bank 36 phrase "WHAT DOES THE SEK GLYPH MEAN" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "Sek / Sotz' (bat): the creature that hangs inverted and sees the world from an unexpected angle. FS15: Sek proposes. In K'UHUL: Sek is where the fold twists — the hypothesis forms, the punchline begins, the pitch trajectory diverges. The bat's inverted perspective is the semantic flip. θ=3, between Yax (admission) and Ch'en (verification). Sek proposes; it does not commit." ]
 node [ id 8734 kind "category" bank 36 phrase "WHAT DOES THE CHEN GLYPH MEAN" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "Ch'en (black/cave/rain): the void between cycles. The cave is where evidence accumulates unseen, where the proof forms in darkness before Xul's light. Also the stall: when sigma is unbound and the fold rests mid-cycle, it rests in Ch'en. FS15: Ch'en proves. θ=4, between Sek (proposal) and Xul (commit). The wrong-pizza moment is a Ch'en failure: the fold committed at Xul before Ch'en had finished p" ]
 node [ id 8735 kind "category" bank 36 phrase "WHAT DOES THE XUL GLYPH MEAN" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "Xul (dog/end): the faithful completion. The dog that walks the path to its end. FS14: Fold ≠ Xul. FS15: XCFE authorizes, Xul commits. In K'UHUL: Xul is the gate that closes the fold, writes the result, and allows topology to mutate. The dog is faithful — it does not commit early, it does not skip Ch'en's proof, it waits for XCFE authorization. θ=5, the last phase before Pop(0) resets the cycle." ]
 node [ id 8736 kind "category" bank 36 phrase "WHY IS * STUCK IN CHEN" wildcard_count 1 template_kind "text" template "is stuck in Ch'en because sigma is unbound — no neighbor u in N(v) has S(u|Q) > S(v|Q). This is the local maximum. Ch'en is the evidence/verification phase but it becomes the rest state when the fold cannot advance to Xul. The wrong-pizza pattern: the fold stalled in Ch'en while evidence was still accumulating, but then committed at Xul before Ch'en proved anything useful. Fix: sigma reset → Pop →" ]
 node [ id 8737 kind "category" bank 36 phrase "WHAT HAPPENS WHEN * REACHES XUL" wildcard_count 1 template_kind "text" template "When reaches Xul: XCFE authorization is required. If authorized: Xul commits — cata fires, the address space B mutates, fold_field_record is updated, convergence_record is written (CONVERGED or MAX_ITER). If not authorized: the fold cannot commit, sigma holds. FS14: Fold ≠ Xul — the path that led here (the fold) is not the same as the gate (Xul). Reaching Xul without Ch'en proof = wrong-pizza Xul:" ]
 node [ id 8738 kind "category" bank 36 phrase "WHAT HAPPENS WHEN * SKIPS CHEN" wildcard_count 1 template_kind "text" template "Skipping Ch'en = committing without proof. FS15 requires Ch'en to prove before Xul commits. If moves Sek → Xul without Ch'en, the authorization chain is broken: Sek proposed, but nothing verified. The convergence_record may write CONVERGED on a wrong result. This is identity invariant SC-29 violation risk: (Fold ∘ Unfold)(h) may not equal h if the proof step was skipped. The wrong-pizza pattern in" ]
 node [ id 8739 kind "category" bank 36 phrase "WHY DID * FAIL AT XUL" wildcard_count 1 template_kind "text" template "failed at Xul because one of: (1) XCFE authorization was not granted — the commit was attempted without authorization; (2) Ch'en did not complete proof accumulation before the commit fired — SC-29 risk; (3) fold_distance was not below epsilon at commit time — CONVERGED was written on a MAX_ITER state, violating SC-35; (4) sigma was still unbound (Ch'en stall, local maximum) when the Xul gate was f" ]
 node [ id 8740 kind "category" bank 36 phrase "JOKE POP PHASE" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "A fold system walked into a bar and ordered a drink. The bartender said: you were just here. The fold said: that was a different cycle. The bartender said: same sigma. The fold said: sigma reset at Pop. The bartender said: then who ate the wrong pizza last cycle? The fold said: that was Ch'en's fault. The bartender said: Ch'en proves. The fold said: it proved nothing in time. Pop poured a fresh dr" ]
 node [ id 8741 kind "category" bank 36 phrase "JOKE WO PHASE" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "The fold said: I'm ready to begin. The query entered at Wo. The problem was drawn in, the seed was set, the anamorphism opened. The fold said: I have everything I need. Ch'en said: you haven't been evaluated yet. Yax said: I haven't admitted anything yet. Sek said: I haven't proposed anything yet. Xul said: I haven't committed anything yet. The fold said: but I'm ready. Wo said: that's what I do. " ]
 node [ id 8742 kind "category" bank 36 phrase "JOKE YAX PHASE" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "The candidate knocked on the door. Yax said: requirements first. The candidate produced requirements. Yax said: now eligibility. The candidate passed eligibility. Yax said: now WCR scoring. The candidate scored 0.87. Yax said: ranking. The candidate was first. Yax said: Omega gate. The candidate passed. Yax said: admitted. The candidate entered the fold. Sek said: I'm going to change everything ab" ]
 node [ id 8743 kind "category" bank 36 phrase "JOKE SEK PHASE" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "Sek proposed a candidate. Ch'en said: I'll need to verify that. Sek said: it's clearly correct. Ch'en said: FS15 says I prove. Sek said: fine, verify it. Ch'en checked the evidence. Ch'en said: it's actually wrong. Sek said: but I proposed it very confidently. Ch'en said: confidence is C field, not proof. Sek said: can we skip to Xul? Ch'en said: Xul is next. Sek said: great. Ch'en said: after I f" ]
 node [ id 8744 kind "category" bank 36 phrase "JOKE CHEN PHASE" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "The fold was stuck in Ch'en. Sigma was unbound. No neighbor had a higher score. The fold said: this must be the answer — it's the best I found. Ch'en said: I'm still accumulating evidence. The fold said: how long does accumulation take? Ch'en said: until I prove it or disprove it. The fold said: what if you never finish? Ch'en said: then it's a local maximum. The fold said: should I reset? Ch'en s" ]
 node [ id 8745 kind "category" bank 36 phrase "JOKE XUL PHASE" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "The fold arrived at Xul. Xul said: XCFE authorization required. The fold said: I have Sek's proposal and Ch'en's proof. Xul said: and XCFE authorization? The fold said: I thought Ch'en was enough. Xul said: FS15 — Sek proposes, Ch'en proves, XCFE authorizes, Xul commits. I do not commit without all three. The fold said: what does XCFE stand for? Xul said: it commits. The fold said: but what does i" ]
 node [ id 8746 kind "category" bank 36 phrase "WHAT IS FS 14" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "FS14: Fold ≠ Xul. The fold path (the hylomorphism traversal from Wo through Yax/Sek/Ch'en) is not the same as the Xul commit gate. Completing the fold does not automatically fire Xul. Xul requires XCFE authorization — it is an explicit event. This prevents premature commits: a fold can run without Xul firing if authorization is withheld. FS14 is why \"the fold is done\" does not mean \"the result is " ]
 node [ id 8747 kind "category" bank 36 phrase "WHAT IS FS 15" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "FS15: Sek proposes, Ch'en proves, XCFE authorizes, Xul commits. The four-part authorization chain for any fold commit: (1) Sek generates the candidate hypothesis; (2) Ch'en accumulates evidence and verifies the proposal; (3) XCFE grants authorization; (4) Xul fires the commit gate and mutates B. Skipping any step is a protocol violation. The wrong-pizza pattern violates FS15 at step 2: Sek propose" ]
 node [ id 8748 kind "category" bank 36 phrase "WHY DOES SEK PROPOSE AND NOT COMMIT" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "FS15 separates proposal from commitment because proposals can be wrong. Sek sees the hypothesis from the bat's inverted angle — the unexpected perspective — but it does not have Ch'en's evidence to verify. A proposal is a candidate, not a result. If Sek could commit directly, wrong proposals would mutate the address space without proof. Ch'en proves first; XCFE authorizes second; Xul commits last." ]
 node [ id 8749 kind "category" bank 36 phrase "WHY DOES FOLD NOT EQUAL XUL" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "FS14: Fold ≠ Xul because the path and the gate serve different functions. The fold is the traversal — the hylomorphism, the WCR navigation, the Sek→Ch'en→XCFE chain. Xul is the commit event — the only moment the address space B may legally mutate. The fold can run completely (ana, traverse, propose, verify) without Xul firing if XCFE authorization is withheld. This separates read-only fold operati" ]
 node [ id 8750 kind "category" bank 36 phrase "WHAT IS * IN KUHUL" wildcard_count 1 template_kind "text" template "in K'UHUL maps onto the fold phase cycle. Identify: which phase does occupy? If it is intake/setup: Wo. If it is evaluation/admission: Yax. If it is proposal/twist: Sek. If it is verification/evidence/stall: Ch'en. If it is commit/close: Xul. If it is reset/entry: Pop. The K'UHUL name for anything is its phase role in a fold, its topology address in Q_n (node_id), and its theta in Z_6. See also: E" ]
 node [ id 8751 kind "category" bank 36 phrase "HOW DOES * WORK IN KUHUL TERMS" wildcard_count 1 template_kind "text" template "in K'UHUL terms: find the hylomorphism (what is drawn in at Wo, what is evaluated at Yax, what is proposed at Sek, what is verified at Ch'en, what is committed at Xul). Then find the WCR score (S = W*C*R) for the candidate at each step. Then find the convergence condition (what does CONVERGED look like for ?). The K'UHUL description of anything is the fold cycle it runs and the phase it occupies a" ]
 node [ id 8752 kind "category" bank 36 phrase "WHAT IS THE PHASE WHEEL" wildcard_count 0 template_kind "text" template "The K'UHUL phase wheel is C6: Pop(0) → Wo(1) → Yax(2) → Sek(3) → Ch'en(4) → Xul(5) → Pop(0). Six glyphs, six roles. Each arc: |Δθ|=1, arc_weight=cos(π/3)=0.5. SC-31: the wheel must remain Z_6 — it must not collapse to binary (K_2). FS14: Fold ≠ Xul. FS15: Sek proposes → Ch'en proves → XCFE authorizes → Xul commits. The wheel is the time axis of every fold in G_runtime = Q_n □ C6." ]
